# PF-7: the build context's ignore list for studio/Dockerfile (BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore in place of the
# context root's .dockerignore; the context is the repository root). An allow-list: everything is left out, then only
# what the API needs at run time is let back in, then installed packages, working files, built output, tests and
# screenshots inside it are left out again. sources/, code/, archive/, .tools/, .git/ and the records never enter.
*
!ai-workers/problem-1-pathway-setup-and-form-filling/prototype
!ai-workers/problem-1-pathway-setup-and-form-filling/official-sources
**/node_modules
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
ai-workers/problem-1-pathway-setup-and-form-filling/prototype/studio/var
ai-workers/problem-1-pathway-setup-and-form-filling/prototype/studio/web/dist
ai-workers/problem-1-pathway-setup-and-form-filling/prototype/studio/tests
ai-workers/problem-1-pathway-setup-and-form-filling/prototype/studio/evidence
ai-workers/problem-1-pathway-setup-and-form-filling/prototype/tests
